{"plan_objective_id": 1, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 1,
  "objective": "Research EDS standard spectrum metadata requirements, EMSA/MAS .msa format specification, and Goldstein et al. requirements",
  "rationale": "Question 1 asks specifically about what metadata must accompany a standard spectrum and cites the EMSA/MAS format spec and Goldstein textbook",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "Found detailed evidence from Newbury & Ritchie 2015, Goldstein et al. 2018, Tong & Mingard 2026, and Newbury & Ritchie 2019 on required metadata. The EMSA/MAS format (ISO 22029) was identified but detailed keyword list not available in retrieved papers - will use expert knowledge for the format specification details.",
  "evaluation": "Multiple citations provide comprehensive list of required metadata for standard spectra."
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 2, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 2,
  "objective": "Research transferability of standard spectra between instruments - detector variation, published methodologies",
  "rationale": "Question 2 asks about cross-instrument standard reuse, detector response differences, and published transfer methodologies",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "Found evidence from multiple sources: Newbury & Ritchie 2015 on stored standards reuse, Newbury & Ritchie 2011/2019 on remote standards and golden detector approach (Alvisi et al. 2006), Tsuji et al. 2010 on detector response modeling including Scholze and Procop, Ritchie et al. 2018 on detector physics variations.",
  "evaluation": "Sufficient evidence gathered on transferability challenges and published methodologies."
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 3, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 3,
  "objective": "Research simulated/synthetic standards accuracy - DTSA-II, NISTMonte, Ritchie's papers",
  "rationale": "Question 3 asks about Monte Carlo simulated standards and their accuracy vs measured standards",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "Found evidence from Newbury & Ritchie 2011 showing DTSA-II simulated vs measured spectra differ by +1.2% (Fe Ka) to +19% (Mg K). Newbury & Ritchie 2015 showed simulated standard analysis of K2496 glass with RDEV within a few percent. Giunto et al. 2025 discusses detector response modeling including ICC. Multiple sources note simulated standards are useful when physical standards unavailable but have limitations at low energy.",
  "evaluation": "Sufficient evidence with numerical accuracy figures."
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 6, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 6,
  "objective": "Research low-kV (5 kV) quantification specifics for Mg Ka in Al matrix",
  "rationale": "Question 6 asks about the specific analytical challenge of trace Mg in Al at low voltage",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "Newbury & Ritchie 2024 tested 263 measurements at 5 keV: >98% within ±5% RDEV, 82% within ±2% RDEV. Multiple papers describe peak overlap issues at low energy, need for careful surface preparation (<50 nm rms roughness), carbon coating effects, detection limit formulas, and standard selection guidance.",
  "evaluation": "Strong quantitative evidence from the 2024 paper plus procedural guidance from multiple sources."
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 4, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 4,
  "objective": "Research physical standards suppliers and certified reference materials for Al, Si, Mg",
  "rationale": "Question 4 asks for specific CRM suppliers, catalog numbers, and Mg standard alternatives",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "Newbury & Ritchie 2024 lists NIST SRMs (470 K411/K412, 479, 481, 482, 1871-1875). They used MgO for Mg, Al2O3 for Al, SiO2 for Si at 5 keV. The paper lists SPI (West Chester, PA) for minerals, Geller Microanalytical Laboratory (Topsfield, MA) for stoichiometric compounds, Alfa Aesar for reagent compounds. Newbury & Ritchie 2015 describes use of MgO, KCl, FeS2, GaP, CaF2 as compound standards. Additional supplier information (Astimex, MAC, Ted Pella) from expert knowledge.",
  "evaluation": "Concrete supplier names and standards identified with sufficient detail from the literature."
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 5, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 5,
  "objective": "Research public repositories of EDS/EPMA spectra",
  "rationale": "Question 5 asks about downloadable spectrum libraries in EMSA format",
  "status": "completed",
  "result": "NIST DTSA-II includes a built-in standards database. The ISO 22029 EMSA/MAS format is the standard format. No large publicly downloadable measured EDS standards library was identified in the literature beyond the DTSA-II internal database. The de-ma.ch web database (Allaz 2024) and Zenodo deposits exist but were not obtainable for detailed review. Remote standards approach described by Newbury & Ritchie.",
  "evaluation": "Key resources identified; limitations in publicly available measured standard spectra documented."
}"}

{"plan_objective_id": 7, "updated_plan_objective_json": "{
  "id": 7,
  "objective": "Create summary artifacts and submit final answer",
  "rationale": "Compile all findings into a comprehensive, well-cited answer",
  "status": "in-progress",
  "result": null,
  "evaluation": null
}"}

